<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Osyp Hladky</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1789–1866</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Osyp Hladky was the last kish otaman of the Danubian Sich, the community of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zaporozhian-cossacks">Zaporozhian Cossacks</a> who settled in the Ottoman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a> delta after 1775. During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russo-turkish-war-1828-1829">Russo-Turkish War</a> of 1828 he defected to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> with part of the Host, after which the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> destroyed the Sich. The Russians settled his followers as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azov">Azov</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cossacks">Cossack</a> Host, which he led for many years.</p></div>
